# DOCS_MAP.md - which docs move with which change

> Documentation is part of the change, not a follow-up. A pull request that
> alters something a reader can observe, and leaves the document describing it
> untouched, has shipped a known-false statement on purpose.

---

## 1. The rules, before the table

**Same change, not a follow-up.** The doc update rides the pull request that
causes it. A follow-up doc task is a task that competes with new work and
loses; the only reliable moment is while the author still knows what changed.

**On doc-versus-code drift, the code wins - and fixing the doc is the change.**
Where a document and the running system disagree, the system is the fact. That
resolves the argument but does not close the defect: the stale sentence is
repaired in the same pass that discovered it, because a known-stale document
left in place is now a deliberate one.

**A skipped doc update is explicit, with a reason. Silence is not allowed.**
"No documentation impact" is a legitimate answer and it is a *stated* answer,
written in the pull request body. The banned state is the one where nobody can
tell whether the docs were considered and dismissed or simply forgotten -
because those two look identical afterwards, and only one of them is fine.

**Every new document registers itself in the same change.** A new file joins
the doc index (and any README or entry-point table the host keeps) in the
commit that creates it. A document nothing links to is a document nobody reads
and nobody maintains; it will be rediscovered later as a contradiction.

**A document that contradicts a newer one is superseded in both directions.**
The old one says what replaced it; the new one says what it replaced. A reader
landing on either must be able to tell which is current without reading both.

---

## 2. The map

Fill one row per change kind this repository actually makes. The right-hand
column is a list of files, not a sentiment.

| Change kind | Doc surfaces that must update in the same change |
|---|---|
| New user-visible surface (screen, page, view) | <INDEX_OR_MENU_TABLE>, a design doc at <DESIGN_DOC_PATH>, the capture/screenshot registry at <CAPTURE_REGISTRY>, the surface-status list at <STATUS_LIST> |
| New or changed API endpoint | The route table in <API_MODULE_OR_DOC>, <API_REFERENCE>, any client or integration doc that enumerates endpoints |
| New or changed command / CLI flag | <CLI_REFERENCE>, the help text itself, <INSTALL_OR_USAGE_DOC> |
| New configuration key or feature flag | <CONFIG_REFERENCE>, the default and its meaning, the revert instruction |
| New background job, timer or scheduled lane | <OPERATIONS_DOC>, the liveness/heartbeat expectations, the on-call or triage notes |
| New event, log line or metric others consume | <EVENT_OR_SCHEMA_DOC> - a consumer cannot subscribe to something undocumented |
| New dependency | <DEPENDENCY_POLICY_DOC>, the licence inventory, the install path |
| Component re-architected or replaced | The architecture doc section, the entry point's current-state block, the plan or roadmap item it closes |
| Component retired | Every document that names it (search, do not recall), plus a superseding note on the doc that replaces it |
| Bug class discovered | `FAILURE_PATTERNS.md` entry **and** the paired `SHIP_CHECKLIST.md` item, in the same change |
| Rule or standing directive issued | `RULES.md` (or the host's equivalent) in the same working chunk it was issued - a directive that exists only in a conversation is a bug |
| Decision made | One decision record, and the superseding marks in both directions |
| <CHANGE_KIND> | <DOC_SURFACES> |

---

## 3. How this gets enforced

Pick at least one mechanism; prose alone decays.

- **Pull-request template line.** One required line: "docs touched: <paths>" or
  "no documentation impact, because <reason>". Cheap, and it makes the skip
  explicit rather than invisible.
- **A mechanical pairing check.** Where a kind has a machine-detectable
  signature - a new route decorator, a new entry in a registry, a new file
  under a known directory - a test can assert the paired doc surface also
  changed. Start with the one kind that has bitten you.
- **Review posture.** The reviewer rejects against this table by name, which is
  only possible because the table lists files rather than intentions.

| Mechanism | Covers which kinds | Enforced by |
|---|---|---|
| <MECHANISM> | <KINDS> | <TEST_OR_TEMPLATE_OR_REVIEW> |

